  "statement_token": "\"A graph is a **homotopy test graph** if its Hom-complexes detect graph colorability through the corresponding homotopy-connectivity bound. **Homotopy-test-graph conjecture.** Every connected bipartite graph is a homotopy test graph. The claim generalizes the known case of connected bipartite graphs equipped with a ${\\\\mathbb Z}_2$-action that flips an edge; the source gives no resolution of the general statement.\"",
